# tighConaill -- Conall's morning, in his cabin: hello
#
# The player wakes in his bed after the landfall. A word of greeting and a word about the
# light; then the scene sends him to the window to draw the curtain (no note: it is just
# what happens when this conversation ends). Read at the player's own pace.
#
# IRISH IS A FIRST DRAFT -- check before shipping.

@file skye/tighConaill
@encounter 0


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
= node 0 — awake
@continue
Ah, there you are.
% Á, tá tú ann.
You slept like a stone. I was beginning to wonder.
% Chodail tú mar chloch. Bhí imní ag teacht orm.

# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
= node 1 — the light
Let us have some light on the matter.
% Cuirimis solas ar an scéal.
